    {
      "role": "user",
      "content": "That's a good way to put it, but I'm still looking for something a bit more \"vivid\" for the younger students in the class. Sometimes purely physical descriptions can feel a bit abstract for them. Do you think there's a more creative or metaphorical way to illustrate that \"pulling\" and \"shoving\" happening at once? Like a way to personify the forces or something to make the mechanics more memorable?",
